# Naming-translation table for use with -rigidbody: it maps a bead's Martini
# label ("BB", "SC1") to the grain name the reduction gave it, which is the
# bead's Martini TYPE ("SP2", "TC3"). Generated by
# data/martini3/prepare_martini3_data.py -- do not edit by hand.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A .rbody rule has to say "+BB" to reach the NEXT
# residue's backbone bead, and it cannot know what residue that is. It cannot
# write the grain name either, because the grain name is the bead's type and
# the backbone type differs by residue: GLY is SP1, ALA SP2, PRO SP2a, HYP
# P1, every other P2.
#
# RigidBodyBuilder resolves exactly this: when an atom is not found under the
# name the .rbody wrote, it translates that name through a table, IN THE
# TARGET RESIDUE'S CONTEXT (RigidBodyBuilder::_translate takes
# target_resname). So "+BB" on an alanine followed by a glycine resolves to
# "SP1". The table it accepts must have EXACTLY ONE ATOM PER RULE --
# _check_translation_is_one_atom_per_rule kills pdb2spn otherwise -- which is
# why reducerules/martini3.grp cannot serve as the table and this file has to
# exist.
#
# ENUMERATING THE NEIGHBOUR INSTEAD DOES NOT WORK, and that was measured, not
# assumed: writing "+P1 +P2 +SP1 +SP2 +SP2a +Q5" in place of "+BB" built 1021
# springs on example/001_GKinase/model.pdb where 982 are right. Four
# side-chain beads carry a backbone type -- THR SC1 is SP1, ASH SC1 SP2, GLH
# SC1 P2, HYP SC1 P1 -- so both the neighbour's backbone AND its first side
# chain answer, and _apply_rule springs every pair it resolves.
#
# INTERIOR RULES ONLY, on purpose: a grain name does not change at a chain
# end (only its force-field key does), and get_rules_for_residue fetches by
# residue name alone, ignoring the position.
#
# It is therefore NOT a reduction. Passing it to a run that would reduce
# would destroy the model: the rule "SP2 ALA BB" looks for an atom named BB,
# and an all-atom structure has none. Use it only with an input that is
# already coarse-grained, where pdb2spn skips the reduction -- see the
# two-step recipe in README.md.
#
SP2 ALA BB
TC3 ALA SC1
P2 CYS BB
TC6 CYS SC1
P2 ASP BB
SQ5n ASP SC1
P2 ASH BB
SP2 ASH SC1
P2 GLU BB
Q5n GLU SC1
P2 GLH BB
P2_2 GLH SC1
P2 PHE BB
SC4 PHE SC1
TC5 PHE SC2
TC5_2 PHE SC3
SP1 GLY BB
P2 HIS BB
TC4 HIS SC1
TN5a HIS SC2
TN6d HIS SC3
P2 HIE BB
TC4 HIE SC1
TN6d HIE SC2
TN5a HIE SC3
P2 HIP BB
TC4 HIP SC1
TP1dq HIP SC2
TP1dq_2 HIP SC3
P2 ILE BB
SC2 ILE SC1
P2 LYS BB
SC3 LYS SC1
SQ4p LYS SC2
P2 LYN BB
SC3 LYN SC1
SN6d LYN SC2
P2 LEU BB
SC2 LEU SC1
P2 MET BB
C6 MET SC1
P2 ASN BB
SP5 ASN SC1
P1 HYP BB
P1_2 HYP SC1
SP2a PRO BB
SC3 PRO SC1
P2 GLN BB
P5 GLN SC1
P2 ARG BB
SC3 ARG SC1
SQ3p ARG SC2
P2 SER BB
TP1 SER SC1
P2 THR BB
SP1 THR SC1
P2 VAL BB
SC3 VAL SC1
P2 TRP BB
TC4 TRP SC1
TN6d TRP SC2
TC5 TRP SC3
TC5_2 TRP SC4
TC5_3 TRP SC5
P2 TYR BB
TC4 TYR SC1
TC5 TYR SC2
TC5_2 TYR SC3
TN6 TYR SC4
